{{!-- THE GM TOOLKIT — the screen-side companion to the GM playbook.

      MODERN LAYOUT ONLY. There are no `{{#if stonetop.classicLayout}}` branches anywhere in
      this sheet and there should never be any: it postdates the icon rail, so it has no
      pre-redesign shape to preserve. That is why the nav goes straight to
      `stonetop.tab-rail-item` rather than through `stonetop.tab-nav-item`, which exists only
      to pick between the two shapes.

      ONE top-level element, as AppV1's `activateListeners` contract requires.

      The header banner is what module/utils/tab-rail.js MEASURES to place the rail: it looks
      for `.stonetop-sheet-header, .steading-header` inside the form and starts the rail 16px
      below whatever it finds. Rename or drop that class and the rail silently falls back to a
      flat 150px from the top of the window.

      THIS SHEET SCROLLS AS ONE UNIT, alone among the actor sheets. The container below is the
      scrollport (stonetop.css, and the sheet's `scrollY` names that class), so the banner
      scrolls off the top with the tab under it rather than staying pinned above it. Anything
      added between the banner and the tab body scrolls away too — there is no pinned region on
      this frame to put it in. --}}
<form class="{{cssClass}} stonetop-gm-toolkit-sheet" autocomplete="off">
	<div class="sheet-wrapper stonetop-gm-toolkit-container">

		<header class="sheet-header stonetop-sheet-header stonetop-gm-toolkit-header">
			<h1 class="stonetop-gm-toolkit-name">{{actor.name}}</h1>
		</header>

		{{!-- The rail's position in the form is arbitrary: tab-rail.js lifts this node onto the
		      window frame before it is ever painted. It is rendered here, inside the form, so
		      that Foundry's Tabs controller finds and binds it normally first. --}}
		<nav class="sheet-tabs tabs stonetop-tab-rail" data-group="primary"
		     aria-label="{{localize "stonetop.sheet.tabs.railLabel"}}">
			{{!-- Homefront leads the rail, above the moves. The playbook's own order puts the move
			      lists first, and this one departs from it deliberately: the moves are what a GM
			      reaches for mid-sentence and are the tab this sheet OPENS on, so the rail costs
			      them nothing by sitting them second, while Homefront is the page you turn to when
			      the party gets home — the start of a stretch of play rather than a moment in
			      one. --}}
			{{> "stonetop.tab-rail-item" tab="homefront" label=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.tabs.homefront")}}
			{{> "stonetop.tab-rail-item" tab="moves"   label=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.tabs.moves")}}
			{{> "stonetop.tab-rail-item" tab="threats" label=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.tabs.threats")}}
			{{> "stonetop.tab-rail-item" tab="sites"   label=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.tabs.sites")}}
			{{> "stonetop.tab-rail-item" tab="wonder"  label=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.tabs.wonder")}}
			{{> "stonetop.tab-rail-item" tab="loop"    label=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.tabs.loop")}}
		</nav>

		<div class="stonetop-sheet-layout stonetop-gm-toolkit-layout stonetop-sheet-layout--own-seam">
			<section class="sheet-body">
				{{> "stonetop.gm-toolkit-tab-homefront"}}
				{{> "stonetop.gm-toolkit-tab-moves"}}
				{{> "stonetop.gm-toolkit-tab-threats"}}
				{{> "stonetop.gm-toolkit-tab-sites"}}
				{{> "stonetop.gm-toolkit-tab-wonder"}}
				{{> "stonetop.gm-toolkit-tab-loop"}}
			</section>
		</div>

	</div>
</form>
